WEBVTT

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.150
Needle ice!

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:17.390
That explains why we're cold.

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:26.860
<i>It's December in the city of Tajimi.</i>

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.500
<i>The weather's quite wintry now.</i>

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:30.600
<i>We're surrounded by mountains,</i>

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:34.300
<i>which means that the summers get hot 
and the winters are piercingly cold.</i>

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:42.880
<i>That's why we use hot water 
for the pottery wheel.</i>

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:46.950
<i>It balances out with the 
coolness of the clay,</i>

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:49.310
<i>creating a uniquely comfortable feeling.</i>

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:11.250
A never-ending loop of coning up and down.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.890
I was wondering about that, too.

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:16.060
Like, how long are you going to do that?!

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:17.850
I totally lost track of time.

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:19.960
That happens sometimes.

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:23.370
Looks like the "Runruu" isn't coming.

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:28.000
Runruu...

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:33.200
It's from Ximena-san.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:34.580
What does it say?

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:35.650
Let's see...

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:38.090
Oh, nice!

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:39.830
But what does it say?

00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:44.000
She said, "I finally finished my piece.
 You should come and see!"

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:21.840
<b>Found It!</b>

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:24.970
<i>And that's how all of us ended up 
at Ximena-san's studio on Tuesday,</i>

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:26.980
<i>when the Kokeigama dojo is closed.</i>

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:29.050
Thanks for coming!

00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:30.200
Come on in.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:34.260
So your piece is under this?

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:35.200
¡Sí!

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:37.210
Here I go!

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:39.680
¡Uno, dos, tres!

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:44.020
Wow!

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:47.700
These are amazing! 
They're so colorful and powerful!

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:50.870
These will make mealtime fun!

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:52.870
Can we pick them up?

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:54.350
Go ahead.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:57.840
It feels so nice in my hands.

00:03:58.220 --> 00:04:00.710
So many suns everywhere.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:04.090
I wanted to express how 
anything put into these dishes

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:06.170
is a blessing from the sun.

00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:09.280
You used the sun as your motif!

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:10.230
That's right!

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:13.590
I love the sun and I love heat.

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:16.360
It's the fuente, the source of vitality.

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:19.610
What's that small set over there?

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:22.130
Right? That is so cute.

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:24.920
This is for making offerings.

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:31.040
When I came to Japan, I learned about 
the nice custom of putting food out

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:33.350
for deceased family members.

00:04:33.350 --> 00:04:36.480
But it seemed so sad to just have 
one bowl on the family altar,

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:38.020
with no side dishes at all.

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:40.750
I thought it would be more fun if they had 
all the same plates as everyone else.

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:42.560
I see.

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:46.570
So that's why you have the 
same set, just smaller.

00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:48.220
That's so nice!

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:52.140
It is.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.600
It's really nice!

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:04.820
Every time I take an offering 
to our family altar,

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:07.290
I also feel that my mother 
might be kind of lonely.

00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:08.900
Right, right?

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:11.680
I made these thinking that 
I wanted to eat together

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:15.280
with my beloved abuelita, my grandmother.

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:18.980
Just looking at these 
miniature dishes is fun,

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:21.280
and I think it's a wonderful concept.

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:26.050
You're going to sell these in 
the showroom next door, right?

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:28.240
Oh, no way.

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:32.550
They said it will be at least another 
two or three years before I can do that.

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:35.840
Oh I see... That's too bad.

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:38.880
But I'll try my best to get there faster.

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:40.570
Keep an eye on me!

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:44.150
But these are so cute...

00:06:05.450 --> 00:06:08.000
Hime-chan, do you still have some time?

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:08.720
Huh?

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:13.600
<b>Café Tokishirou</b>

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:13.610
I've been wondering about something.

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:18.530
How is she doing? Is she 
able to spread her wings?

00:06:18.530 --> 00:06:20.430
She seems to be doing fine.

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:23.050
It seems that lately she's only 
coning her clay up and down

00:06:23.050 --> 00:06:24.860
and can't seem to really move forward.

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:26.120
Oh, my.

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:33.610
I wonder if I turned her into someone 
who can't really let out her true self...

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:34.810
What?

00:06:34.810 --> 00:06:37.370
What's that supposed to mean?

00:06:37.950 --> 00:06:41.340
I asked a lot of her at a time 
when she wanted to play the most,

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:43.860
and now holding back has 
become normal for her...

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:50.860
Limited-time-only sale...

00:06:50.860 --> 00:06:51.880
Limited-time-only sale...

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:53.920
Himeno?

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:55.600
Hey, dad!

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:57.880
Did you...

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:00.190
I did!

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:02.630
The last half-off chicken is mine!

00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:03.610
Nice!

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:07.200
Even back in middle school.

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:09.450
You would think she'd want 
to be out with friends,

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:11.950
but instead, she was always 
helping out around the house.

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:16.450
I think that's also why she 
joined the home economics club.

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:17.800
You think so?

00:07:19.490 --> 00:07:23.110
I'm glad she's turned out 
so considerate, but...

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:28.010
I think that might be the reason that she 
can't make a piece to put on that shelf.

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:29.830
You're overthinking it!

00:07:29.830 --> 00:07:32.050
That girl is so strong.

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:36.360
Hey, you should be having this conversation 
at a parent-teacher conference.

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:39.780
You are completely right! I am sorry.

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:41.410
What would you like to drink next?

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:44.470
I'll take a highball, on the strong side.

00:07:46.830 --> 00:07:49.330
Wow, it's so bright!

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:56.780
The lights are so pretty!

00:07:56.780 --> 00:07:59.360
And even prettier during 
cherry blossom season!

00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:02.590
Really? Then I'm looking forward 
to next year's spring.

00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:07.970
So here I go.

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:14.590
This might sound impertinent, but 
I think you should make a mug next.

00:08:15.530 --> 00:08:16.240
Huh?

00:08:17.910 --> 00:08:20.030
I don't think you've realized it,

00:08:20.030 --> 00:08:23.740
but the only thing you 
haven't made yet is a mug.

00:08:25.930 --> 00:08:30.710
<i>Somewhere in my heart, I had thought 
that if I made the same item as my mom,</i>

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:32.400
<i>I could never compete with her...</i>

00:08:32.850 --> 00:08:35.620
<i>Even though there's no reason 
to think of it like that.</i>

00:08:36.310 --> 00:08:41.610
I was always thinking that those were 
something really special to you.

00:08:41.610 --> 00:08:42.480
Yeah.

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:45.470
But I think you could make one now.

00:08:45.470 --> 00:08:50.100
One made by Hime-chan, according to 
Hime-chan, a Hime-chan colored mu-choo!

00:08:51.910 --> 00:08:55.540
Oh geez, Nao-chan, you're too cute!

00:08:57.200 --> 00:09:00.140
But you're right.

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:04.650
I feel like I could make one now.

00:09:05.170 --> 00:09:06.990
Thank you, Nao-chan.

00:09:06.990 --> 00:09:08.620
I didn't do anything.

00:09:23.050 --> 00:09:24.100
I'm home—

00:09:24.840 --> 00:09:26.530
Welcome back.

00:09:26.530 --> 00:09:27.300
Heya.

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:29.740
Oh, hello!

00:09:29.740 --> 00:09:30.930
It's been a while.

00:09:30.930 --> 00:09:33.750
Grandma, I'll change and 
then I can take your place.

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:36.170
Really? Well, thank you.

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:40.900
Wow, it's really a party in here.

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:43.440
I mean, this is my third one!

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:47.170
We were talking about that time when 
your mother made that monument.

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:48.410
Really?

00:09:49.070 --> 00:09:52.810
The first time you saw that monument, 
you wrote a poem about it.

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:54.260
A poem?

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:56.400
What are you talking about?

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:59.560
Oh, yeah! I remember that! 
You were in the literature club.

00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:02.560
Oh, you were in the literature club!

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:03.730
No, we're done!

00:10:03.730 --> 00:10:04.920
This topic is done!

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:06.410
So what kind of poem was it?

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:08.330
I said, it's over!

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:09.440
Why, though?

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:11.240
I liked it.

00:10:11.240 --> 00:10:13.640
"Wings born in the wind,"

00:10:13.640 --> 00:10:15.620
"I have become an angel."

00:10:16.030 --> 00:10:20.010
Senpai, stop right there, or I'll 
never set foot in this store again.

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:21.850
I'm sorry, I'm sorry!

00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:26.420
Is this the "cringey past"
you mentioned before?

00:10:32.930 --> 00:10:34.950
I don't really know...

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:39.310
Looking back now, it seems like 
I was just hyped up late at night

00:10:39.310 --> 00:10:42.660
and completely made light of literature...

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:49.840
It's embarrassing because all I did was 
naïvely write down my unfiltered emotions.

00:10:49.840 --> 00:10:51.960
That happens a lot with teenagers.

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:57.470
But it's impressive that you got over 
that and became a Japanese teacher.

00:10:57.470 --> 00:10:58.790
This!

00:10:58.790 --> 00:11:01.340
You never know which way 
someone's going to go.

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:05.230
I never even thought about becoming a 
teacher until the second year of high school.

00:11:05.230 --> 00:11:08.170
So how did that even happen?

00:11:08.170 --> 00:11:11.490
Well, one of my friends who was working 
on the school's literature anthology

00:11:11.490 --> 00:11:13.810
included one of my pieces without asking.

00:11:15.340 --> 00:11:18.740
I didn't feel confident 
about that poem at all.

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:21.710
It was just something where 
I put my feelings down on the page

00:11:21.710 --> 00:11:23.750
without any decoration.

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:30.230
But despite of that, it became 
something special inside me.

00:11:31.440 --> 00:11:35.740
Our Japanese teacher read it and 
she gave me some earnest praise.

00:11:36.310 --> 00:11:41.330
She said the way I considered my 
subject was so gentle and good.

00:11:44.660 --> 00:11:49.380
That gave me some confidence and it inspired 
me to not just write from the gut,

00:11:49.380 --> 00:11:51.950
but to actually study writing.

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:55.130
That was what led me to become a teacher.

00:11:55.570 --> 00:11:58.340
My goal now is to try to 
be like that teacher;

00:11:58.340 --> 00:12:04.560
I hope to find a small seed of greatness 
and help my students foster that.

00:12:05.010 --> 00:12:07.600
You should be grateful to that friend who exposed

00:12:07.600 --> 00:12:09.310
your embarrassing poem to everybody.

00:12:09.310 --> 00:12:10.360
You had to put it that way!

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:13.650
But it's true, though.

00:12:13.650 --> 00:12:16.070
Showing someone your stuff is important.

00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:20.360
That will broaden your horizon.

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:21.840
That's true.

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:23.420
Another oolong tea, please.

00:12:23.420 --> 00:12:24.620
Coming right up.

00:12:25.790 --> 00:12:27.050
That's it.

00:12:27.750 --> 00:12:28.880
That's exactly it.

00:12:29.920 --> 00:12:31.870
I'm starting to see it!

00:12:37.590 --> 00:12:38.890
I got it!

00:12:39.590 --> 00:12:40.810
I got it!

00:12:42.610 --> 00:12:44.490
I'm going now!

00:12:45.270 --> 00:12:46.120
Nao-chan!

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:47.270
Nao-chan!

00:12:47.270 --> 00:12:48.230
Hime-chan?

00:12:48.230 --> 00:12:48.800
What's up?

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:51.010
Morning! Let's run, Nao-chan!

00:12:51.010 --> 00:12:52.550
But why?

00:12:52.550 --> 00:12:54.300
Just because!

00:13:00.360 --> 00:13:04.440
<i>Suddenly a lot of things have 
started moving inside me.</i>

00:13:05.060 --> 00:13:06.290
<i>Here I go!</i>

00:13:06.290 --> 00:13:08.730
<i>I'm going to make that mug!</i>

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:27.410
The bob-haired girl is being weird.

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:35.270
<b>Mini-Mini Pottery Club</b>

00:14:27.410 --> 00:14:31.080
But I've got a good feeling 
about this weird.

00:14:31.080 --> 00:14:33.080
Don't fret, father.

00:14:33.420 --> 00:14:36.140
Next time, "Freedom, Future, Sparkle."

00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:39.930
<b>Next Time:</b>

00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:39.930
<b>Freedom, Future, Sparkle</b>

00:14:36.140 --> 00:14:39.610
I don't know why, but for some 
reason, my soul's on fire!
